\f2 \cf0 At that moment every stasis cupboard in the Primary Trade Dominion malfunctioned. Food instantaneously spoiled and turned to dust. At Food and Drug Administration Headquarters, urgent meetings at the highest level were convened. For the first time in it\'92s history something had seriously gone wrong with stasis technology. Sure, a few cupboards had blown fuses and had other minor issues over the years, but never such a catastrophe. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I don\'92t believe this is some sort of accident or natural event,\'94 opined Halverson Tentries III, L.5. Maintenance Technician. \'93Someone is fucking with us.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93They clearly don\'92t understand the technology and could do some real damage.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93That is an understatement. We are talking about the end of time.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Listen to Mr Worse-case-Scenario\'94 nbnbnbn \'93It would take some seriously reckless action to mess with space-time.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We can\'92t assume no danger and hope for the best.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Just as long as they are not dumb enough to centrifuge the stasis circuitry.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No-one would be that moronic.\'94
\f1 \

